step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Start with a baseline mean of the full pool to gauge performance before trying more sophisticated combos.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Evaluate a weighted combination using inverse error to see if weighting improves over plain mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it improves over mean and weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Try a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if removing extremes improves SMAPE.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Try a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle w1 on the full pool to see if a meta‑model weight improves over inverse_error.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a dba combination on the full pool to see if it outperforms the current weighted best.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test the best single model (ARIMA) to see if a single model outperforms the weighted ensemble for this noisy series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a weighted ensemble on a reduced, more stable pool (pool1) to see if removing noisy models improves SMAPE over the single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse_error combination on pool2 to see if adding ETS improves performance over pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Try a weighted ensemble on pool3 (ARIMA, ETS, THETA, rf, DWT_catboost, FT_catboost) using inverse_error weights to see if a focused subset beats the single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean of a smaller, more relevant pool (pool1) to see if reducing model noise improves SMAPE over the full pool mean.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on pool2 to see if it beats the best single ARIMA on this noisy series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

